# Go notes (9x9, Black vs KataGo human-style) — READ FIRST

See `games.md` for the per-game log. Update both files after every game.

## Ladder status
- Game 1: vs 8k, lost W+14 (Black 37 area vs White 44 + komi 7).
- Next suggestion: stay at 8k (or try 10k) until winning, then climb ~2 ranks per win.

## Key facts
- Komi 7, area scoring: Black needs >= 44 of 81 points to win. Count areas mid-game!
  In game 1 Black had a fine-looking center but only ~37 points -> center walls do not
  score on their own. Each side of the board matters.
- Area scoring: playing inside opponent's territory late is free (no point cost), so
  probing invasions at the end costs nothing.
- Opponent passes when the game is settled; engine removes dead stones itself.

## Lessons (game 1)
1. CHECK LIBERTIES OF MY OWN STONES before every move, especially after the opponent
   plays adjacent. I lost G4 because White's G5 put it in atari (1 lib) and I didn't notice.
2. Opening: after 1.E5 White played C4 and G3 (low 3rd-line stones on two sides).
   My D3 / G4 approach let White settle both sides AND later invade the upper-left (C7).
   White ended with the whole left edge + right edge. Black's center wall was too
   thick/inefficient. Better: take territory on a side yourself instead of only pressing
   (e.g. answer C4 with C6/D6-type moves that also claim the top, or take a corner).
3. Don't throw in cutting stones (B7, B4) that end up with 1-2 liberties inside the
   opponent's strong area; they just die and give the opponent tempo. Read 2-3 moves first.
4. When behind on count by 15+, the only hope is to kill — identify the weakest enemy
   group EARLY (before it settles), not at the end.
5. A 1-wide strip of 4 on the edge (straight four) is alive; don't waste moves there.

## Process checklist each move
- What did the opponent's last move threaten? (Count libs of all my groups next to it.)
- Any of my groups at 1-2 libs? Any of theirs?
- Rough count: who is ahead? If behind, play bigger/more aggressive.
